\fs32\b Options\b0\fs20\par
\par
Options allow you to change the way WinBMD2 looks and behaves while you are transcribing.\par
\par
Your choices are remembered by WinBMD2 and will normally remain in use the next time the program is started.\par
\par
\fs24\b Opening Options\b0\fs20\par
Use the Options command above the transcription grid to display the available settings.\par
\par
Options can also be opened from the Header Form before starting or opening a batch.\par
\par
\fs24\b Automatically displaying scans\b0\fs20\par
You can choose whether WinBMD2 should automatically locate and display the scan associated with the current transcription.\par
\par
When this option is enabled, WinBMD2 will normally display the appropriate scan automatically when sufficient information is available to identify it.\par
\par
If it is disabled, scans can still be displayed whenever required using the Scan commands.\par
\par
\fs24\b Transcription settings\b0\fs20\par
Other options control aspects of how information is entered into the transcription grid and how WinBMD2 assists you while transcribing.\par
\par
These settings allow you to adjust WinBMD2 to suit the way you prefer to work.\par
\par
\fs24\b Appearance\b0\fs20\par
Where appearance choices are available, they affect the way WinBMD2 is displayed without changing the transcription itself.\par
\par
Changing an option does not alter the information already entered in the transcription unless the option specifically relates to the way that information is processed.\par
